  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="dd69-b3db-89ef-4269" name="End of Persia (Alexander the Great) - List Notes" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false">
      <description>THE END OF PERSIA ARMY LIST 401-330 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.92-94). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25% (the Army General is either the Great King or a Satrapal General). Persians at least 25%. Levies up to 50%. Greek Mercenaries up to 25%. Allies and War machines up to 15%.
The minimum size for a regiment is five models. There is no upper limit on most units although scythed chariots are limited to a maximum of four models per 2,000 pts. One model in each unit may be upgraded to Leader (+5 pts), Standard Bearer (+5 pts) and Musician (+5 pts). Greek Mercenaries: the Later Persian army may have a Polemarch and any units from the Greek Mercenaries list except Greek League Hoplites; Persian characters may not join Greek units (documented only, no pick list). Allies (Bithynians from the Thracian list - 0-1 Chieftain, no rhomphaia or Shamans; Eastern Satrapies if the Great King is present: 0-1 Parapamisidae cavalry, Indian cavalry and Hereditary Infantry, and 0-1 elephant) are documented only. Lykians and Carians are listed as units. Optional rules: Prepared Ground (River Defence, Cleared Ground) and Scythed Chariots Out of Control are not built; Historical Persian Characters (Darius III, Nabarzanes, Bessus) are documented in the book only. Not enforced: one Satrap per Persian regiment, Levies, Noble or Shock cavalry unit; one light ballista per Persian infantry unit; every second unit options; at most four scythed chariots per 2,000 pts; the Great King/Satrapal General restrictions.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[The End of Persia]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Persians: at least 25%
  Levies: up to 50%
  Allies &amp; War Machines: up to 15%
  THE END OF PERSIA ARMY LIST 401-330 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.92-94). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25% (the Army General is either the Great King or a Satrapal General). Persians at least 25%. Levies up to 50%. Greek Mercenaries up to 25%. Allies and War machines up to 15%.
The minimum size for a regiment is five models. There is no upper limit on most units although scythed chariots are limited to a maximum of four models per 2,000 pts. One model in each unit may be upgraded to Leader (+5 pts), Standard Bearer (+5 pts) and Musician (+5 pts). Greek Mercenaries: the Later Persian army may have a Polemarch and any units from the Greek Mercenaries list except Greek League Hoplites; Persian characters may not join Greek units (documented only, no pick list). Allies (Bithynians from the Thracian list - 0-1 Chieftain, no rhomphaia or Shamans; Eastern Satrapies if the Great King is present: 0-1 Parapamisidae cavalry, Indian cavalry and Hereditary Infantry, and 0-1 elephant) are documented only. Lykians and Carians are listed as units. Optional rules: Prepared Ground (River Defence, Cleared Ground) and Scythed Chariots Out of Control are not built; Historical Persian Characters (Darius III, Nabarzanes, Bessus) are documented in the book only. Not enforced: one Satrap per Persian regiment, Levies, Noble or Shock cavalry unit; one light ballista per Persian infantry unit; every second unit options; at most four scythed chariots per 2,000 pts; the Great King/Satrapal General restrictions.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
